Verified against this repo's own source:
  bool hostonly = s->m2exec && s->m2hostsem && nvkvm_m2_is_user_ce(s, s->chan_client);
  (src/qemu/nvkvm_gpu_emul.c:5555)
⇒ m2hostsem gates HOST OWNERSHIP of the semaphore, NOT the forge. m2hostsem=0 ⇒
hostonly == false ⇒ THE CPU FORGE RUNS.
⊘ And nvkvm_m2_is_user_ce can NEVER be a GR client (:7855 guards it explicitly), so
on the COMPUTE plane hostonly is false AT EVERY FLAG SETTING and the software
completion write at :5726 is UNCONDITIONAL.

★ SCOPE THE CORRECTION — it is narrower than it looks. This does NOT refute that the
host GR engine EXECUTED the guest's pushbuffer. It refutes the INFERENCE that the C's
guest therefore WAITED ON HARDWARE for its completion: it read a value the CPU had
already written.
⇒ The C remains an oracle for GR ENGINE EXECUTION and is NOT an oracle for the
COMPLETION PATH.

⚠ Same class as the miscitation this file already records: A FLAG'S NAME READ AS ITS
PREDICATE. Read the definition site, not the name.

